From: esp32-fx <local@esp32-fx.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] xtensa: reserve deterministic PSRAM arena for WAMR

The no-MMU allocator cannot reliably reconstruct a physically contiguous
1 MiB block after networking and filesystem activity.  Reserve the final
1088 KiB of PSRAM during memblock setup: 64 KiB for bounded native response
streaming followed by 1 MiB for the guest linear-memory ceiling.

The esp32-fx supervisor verifies this exact device-tree reservation before
using the direct PSRAM addresses.  This trades idle general-purpose memory
for deterministic repeatable Wasm launches; it is specific to the 8 MiB
PSRAM deployment-host profile.

---
 arch/xtensa/boot/dts/esp32s3-reterminal-e1001.dts | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/xtensa/boot/dts/esp32s3-reterminal-e1001.dts b/arch/xtensa/boot/dts/esp32s3-reterminal-e1001.dts
index 333333333333..444444444444 100644
--- a/arch/xtensa/boot/dts/esp32s3-reterminal-e1001.dts
+++ b/arch/xtensa/boot/dts/esp32s3-reterminal-e1001.dts
@@ -9,6 +9,17 @@
 		device_type = "memory";
 		reg = <0x3d800000 0x00800000>;
 	};
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <1>;
+		#size-cells = <1>;
+		ranges;
+
+		fx_wamr_arena: fx-wamr-arena@3def0000 {
+			/* 64 KiB native stream + 1 MiB guest linear memory. */
+			reg = <0x3def0000 0x00110000>;
+		};
+	};
+
 };
 
 &gpio_in_mux {
